## Phoenix starts pricing decision and embedding spans in cost tracking

Source: GitHub — https://github.com/Arize-ai/phoenix/releases/tag/arize-phoenix-v22.0.0
Published: 2026-11-20
Channel: github

Arize Phoenix is an open-source observability platform that records and evaluates the steps of LLM applications. Cost tracking in Phoenix uses token counts and per-token prices to report spending on traces. A stable server release extends that work to two more kinds of records that appear in traces: decision spans, which capture an individual model decision, and embedding spans, which capture an embedding operation that turns text into a numeric vector.

The release notes add cost calculation for both span types. They also put model types into the cost manifest and sync prices through LiteLLM, including Gemini models that LiteLLM lists only under a Gemini prefix. The generative model's type is exposed through GraphQL, the API used to query Phoenix, and a related fix makes that type immutable once it is set.

Phoenix's migration notes say no manual steps are needed: the server now calculates costs for decision and embedding spans. Operators who watch project and trace cost totals should confirm, after they upgrade, that decision and embedding work is included in those totals and that each model is classified as the type they expect.

Why it matters: If you use Phoenix cost totals for agent or retrieval traffic, upgrade and compare a trace that includes decision or embedding work against the prior totals, and check that each generative model has the intended type.

