## OpenInference can also write OpenTelemetry GenAI attributes on traces

Source: GitHub — https://github.com/Arize-ai/openinference/releases/tag/%40arizeai/openinference-core%402.9.0
Published: 2026-11-20
Channel: github

OpenInference is an instrumentation library that records LLM and agent calls as trace spans, usually with its own attribute names. Some collectors and backends expect OpenTelemetry's GenAI semantic conventions, a shared set of gen_ai attribute names for model and agent telemetry, and may not see those fields on OpenInference spans alone.

A stable OpenInference core release adds an experimental option, enableGenAISemconv, and a matching environment variable, OPENINFERENCE_ENABLE_GENAI_SEMCONV. When the option is enabled, spans created through OITracer, OpenInference's tracer, also emit those GenAI attributes. The attributes are derived at the end of the span from the span's masked OpenInference attributes, so values that were already redacted stay redacted. The same conversion is also exported as a helper, getGenAIAttributes, for callers that need the mapped fields directly.

The notes describe the feature as experimental. Teams that need both OpenInference detail and GenAI-shaped attributes can turn the option on in a non-production tracer first and compare a sample span to confirm the mapped fields match what their collector expects.

Why it matters: If your pipeline already stores OpenInference spans but a downstream tool looks for gen_ai attributes, enable the experimental option in a test tracer and compare one span before turning it on more widely.

